cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it, and cite the primary sources it rests on."
title: "odu-core: the 256 Odù Ifá as a canonical byte mapping"
abstract: >-
  A verified mapping between the 256 Odù Ifá and the 256 values of a byte,
  with Yorùbá orthography preserved. All 16 principal figures are verified
  against Bascom (1969). Seniority follows the southwestern Yorùbá order;
  the Ifẹ variant is recorded alongside it.
type: dataset
version: 1.0.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/timeyinallout-cloud/odu-core"
keywords:
  - Odù Ifá
  - Ifá divination
  - Yorùbá
  - heritage computing
  - binary encoding
authors:
  - family-names: Bemi
    given-names: Timeyin

references:
  - type: book
    title: "Ifa Divination: Communication Between Gods and Men in West Africa"
    authors:
      - family-names: Bascom
        given-names: William R.
    year: 1969
    publisher:
      name: Indiana University Press
    notes: >-
      The primary source. Table 1 p. 4 and Table 3 column B p. 48 verify all
      16 principal figures and the seniority order used here. Cite this
      alongside the dataset — the dataset is a transcription, not a discovery.
  - type: book
    title: "Sixteen Great Poems of Ifá"
    authors:
      - family-names: Abimbọla
        given-names: Wande
    year: 1975
    publisher:
      name: "OAU Centre for Linguistic and Historical Studies by Oral Tradition, Niamey"
    notes: >-
      Frequently miscited as a UNESCO publication. UNESCO funded it; the OAU
      published it. Recorded but not yet consulted.
